{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q410298","formula":"C₄₂H₆₅N₁₃O₁₀","hill":"C42H65N13O10","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":42.0,"H":65.0,"N":13.0,"O":10.0},"names":{"en":"Saralasin"},"descriptions":{"en":"Saralasin is a competitive angiotensin II receptor antagonist with partial agonistic activity. The aminopeptide sequence for saralasin differs from angiotensin II at three sites: At position 1, sarcosine replaces aspartic acid, thereby increasing the affinity for vascular smooth muscle AT II receptors and making sara resistant to degradation by aminopeptidases. At position 5, isoleucine is replaced by valine At position 8, phenylalanine is replaced by alanine which leads to a smaller stimulatory effect."},"fame":9,"pubchemCid":6324663,"mass":912.0,"charge":0,"smiles":"C[C@@H](C(=O)O)NC(=O)[C@@H]1CCCN1C(=O)[C@H](CC2=CN=CN2)NC(=O)[C@H](C(C)C)NC(=O)[C@H](CC3=CC=C(C=C3)O)NC(=O)[C@H](C(C)C)NC(=O)[C@H](CCCN=C(N)N)NC(=O)CNC","inchikey":"PFGWGEPQIUAZME-NXSMLHPHSA-N","iupac":"(2S)-2-[[(2S)-1-[(2S)-2-[[(2S)-2-[[(2S)-2-[[(2S)-2-[[(2S)-5-(diaminomethylideneamino)-2-[[2-(methylamino)acetyl]amino]pentanoyl]amino]-3-methylbutanoyl]amino]-3-(4-hydroxyphenyl)propanoyl]amino]-3-methylbutanoyl]amino]-3-(1H-imidazol-5-yl)propanoyl]pyrrolidine-2-carbonyl]amino]propanoic acid","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"6324663","atoms":130,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":11.028,"y":1.821,"z":-0.578,"el":"C"},{"x":10.059,"y":1.413,"z":-1.676,"el":"C"},{"x":10.806,"y":1.267,"z":-3.001,"el":"C"},{"x":11.168,"y":0.215,"z":-3.509,"el":"O"},{"x":11.093,"y":2.448,"z":-3.583,"el":"O"},{"x":9.439,"y":0.124,"z":-1.355,"el":"N"},{"x":8.18,"y":-0.174,"z":-1.844,"el":"C"},{"x":7.466,"y":0.657,"z":-2.397,"el":"O"},{"x":7.746,"y":-1.637,"z":-1.605,"el":"C"},{"x":